## Separate Carrier Stage

After checking Baskets 1 through 17 and accounting for 4,800 µL liquid stocks plus 2.640 g saturated Ambrofix stock, add **ethanol 96% q.s. to 30.00 mL final volume**. Ethanol is a technical carrier stage, not Basket 18.

Do not add the historical fixed 24,600 µL ethanol charge. Do not add extra DEP, DPG, TEC, IPM, Ambrofix, Ambrox Super, or superamber to compensate numerically. Record the actual q.s. ethanol amount and the finished bottle mass.

## Quantitation and Acceptance Boundary

The mass-dose replacement preserves the former amber-row nominal active mass to within 3.0%, but Ambrofix and Ambrox Super remain distinct products. Stock density is unknown, so active µL, strict Ambrofix ppm and OAV remain HOLD. The old S35-F2 Ambrox pipeline result cannot be relabeled as an F3 Ambrofix result.

Inspect the trial immediately and at 24 and 48 hours for clarity, sediment, crystallization, haze, or phase separation. Those observations test physical repeatability only; they do not establish safety or shelf stability.

No physical liking, similarity, performance, safety, stability, market success, or release claim is authorized by this protocol. A controlled Ambrox-versus-Ambrofix comparison remains necessary before calling the successor equivalent or more hedonic.
